---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Why Open Source | Why Ecosoft"
  description="Open source isn't a compromise — it's a competitive advantage. Addressing the biggest objections to open-source ERP for enterprise organisations."
>


  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 44rem;">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why Open Source</p>
        <h1>Open source isn't a compromise. It's a competitive advantage.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
          This page directly addresses the most common objection: <em>"Is open source reliable enough for enterprise?"</em>
          The short answer is yes — and the evidence is overwhelming.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MYTH VS REALITY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Myth vs. Reality</p>
        <h2>What decision-makers believe — and what's actually true</h2>
      </header>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem;">
        <article class="info-card" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; align-items: start;">
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ef4444; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">The Myth</p>
            <h3 style="color: var(--text);">Open Source Means Risky</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65;">
              Many decision-makers assume that paid, proprietary software is inherently safer or more
              reliable than open source. If you pay for it, someone is accountable. If it's free,
              anyone can break it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: #16a34a; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">The Reality</p>
            <h3 style="color: var(--text);">Open Source Means Transparent</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65;">
              SAP runs on Linux. Netflix runs on open source. The Thai government's most advanced science
              agency, NSTDA, replaced SAP with Ecosoft's Odoo implementation in 2018 — and has never
              looked back. Open source means every line of code is auditable, not hidden behind a
              vendor's black box.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; align-items: start;">
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ef4444; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">The Myth</p>
            <h3 style="color: var(--text);">Open Source Has No Support</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65;">
              If something breaks, who do you call? With proprietary software you have a vendor contract.
              With open source, you're on your own.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: #16a34a; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">The Reality</p>
            <h3 style="color: var(--text);">You Call Ecosoft</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65;">
              Ecosoft provides post-implementation support, SLA-based maintenance, and system evolution
              services. The difference: with us, you're not locked in. You can switch to any other
              developer at any time — because you own the code and the documentation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; align-items: start;">
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ef4444; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">The Myth</p>
            <h3 style="color: var(--text);">Free Software Means Low Quality</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65;">
              The software is free, so it can't be as good as software that costs thousands of dollars
              per user per year. You get what you pay for.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: #16a34a; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">The Reality</p>
            <h3 style="color: var(--text);">The Community Enforces Quality</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65;">
              OCA modules are peer-reviewed by an international community of expert developers. The bar
              for merging code is higher than most proprietary vendors maintain internally. Ecosoft
              builds to OCA standards — not because it's required, but because our clients deserve it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ECONOMICS -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Economics</p>
        <h2>No licence = more budget for excellence</h2>
        <p>
          A typical SAP or Oracle implementation requires six- to seven-figure annual licence payments —
          before you pay a single consultant. Odoo Community Edition and ERPNext are 100% free. That
          budget stays in your organisation.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="cards-grid">
        <article class="info-card pillar-card">
          <span class="pillar-number">฿0</span>
          <h3>Software Licence Cost</h3>
          <p>Odoo Community Edition and ERPNext are both 100% open source. Zero per-user fees, zero annual renewals, zero licence costs forever.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card pillar-card">
          <span class="pillar-number">60%</span>
          <h3>Lower 5-Year TCO</h3>
          <p>Open-source ERP with a quality implementor typically delivers 60–80% lower total cost of ownership compared to SAP or Microsoft Dynamics over five years.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card pillar-card">
          <span class="pillar-number">100%</span>
          <h3>Budget for Quality</h3>
          <p>The licence savings go into better implementation, more custom modules, deeper training — the things that actually determine whether ERP succeeds or fails.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card pillar-card">
          <span class="pillar-number">∞</span>
          <h3>Future Flexibility</h3>
          <p>No vendor lock-in means you can upgrade, extend, migrate, or hand the system to any developer. Your ERP investment grows with you indefinitely.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ODOO CE + OCA vs ENTERPRISE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our Choice of Platform</p>
        <h2>Odoo CE + OCA vs Odoo Enterprise</h2>
        <p>
          Ecosoft works exclusively with Odoo Community Edition, enhanced by OCA modules — not Odoo
          Enterprise. Here's why that choice matters to you.
        </p>
      </header>
      <table class="pricing-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Factor</th>
            <th class="col-featured">Odoo CE + OCA (Ecosoft)</th>
            <th>Odoo Enterprise</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Licence Cost</strong></td>
            <td>฿0 — fully open source</td>
            <td>฿5,000–฿20,000+ per user per year</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Source Code Access</strong></td>
            <td>Full — you own everything</td>
            <td>Restricted — Enterprise modules are proprietary</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Thai Localisation</strong></td>
            <td>120+ OCA Thai modules by Ecosoft</td>
            <td>Limited — requires enterprise add-ons</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Module Quality</strong></td>
            <td>OCA peer-reviewed international standard</td>
            <td>Vendor-controlled, proprietary review</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Community</strong></td>
            <td>Global OCA community — hundreds of contributors</td>
            <td>Odoo SA controlled</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Vendor Lock-In</strong></td>
            <td>None — any developer can work with your code</td>
            <td>High — dependent on Odoo SA pricing and roadmap</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-strip">
    <div class="container cta-strip-grid">
      <div class="cta-strip-item">
        <h3>Still have questions about open source?</h3>
        <p>Talk to one of our consultants — no sales pitch, just honest answers to your concerns.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-white">Ask Us Anything</a>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-strip-item">
        <h3>Read the Odoo vs ERPNext comparison</h3>
        <p>Both are excellent open-source platforms. Find out which is the better fit for your business.</p>
        <a href="/resources/odoo-vs-erpnext" class="btn btn-teal-outline">Compare Platforms →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
